Spell <ws2tcpip.h> as the header is named.

FileZilla includes <Ws2tcpip.h>, which only a case-insensitive file system
resolves; mingw-w64 names it ws2tcpip.h, so a Linux host cannot find it even
when cross-compiling for Windows. Lower case works everywhere, Windows and
C++Builder included. The only such system include in the transformed trees,
so a patch rather than a rule.

--- a/source/filezilla/AsyncSocketEx.h	2026-10-11 13:22:26.423761794 -0300
+++ b/source/filezilla/AsyncSocketEx.h	2026-10-11 13:22:26.425882469 -0300
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@
 #define FD_FORCEREAD (1<<15)
 //---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 #include <winsock2.h>
-#include <Ws2tcpip.h>
+#include <ws2tcpip.h>
 //---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 class CAsyncSocketExHelperWindow;
 class CAsyncSocketExLayer;
